\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Falls After Bank Of Japan Policy Moves\b0\par\par\uc2 803 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2013\par 21:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 By Carla Mozee and Barbara Kollmeyer, MarketWatch\par \par \uc2 LOS ANGELES (MarketWatch) -- The Japanese yen jumped against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, strengthening as investors learned that planned asset purchases by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will start later than anticipated.\par \par \uc2 The greenback also lost ground against the euro following a better-than-expected survey of German sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the U.S. dollar (USDJPY) fell 1% to 88.70 yen, down from Yen89.71 in late Monday trading. The euro (EURJPY) also dropped, changing hands at Yen118.10 compared with Yen119.56 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  adopted a target to reach a 2% increase in consumer prices, and said it will conduct asset purchases on an open-ended basis in a bid to bolster monetary stimulus. Prime Minister Shinzo Abe, who was elected in December, has urged the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  help spur growth in the world's third-largest economy and end decades of falling prices.\par \par \uc2 Initially reacting to the announcements from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar popped higher to around Yen90.18 before dropping back.\par \par \uc2 The open-ended asset-purchase program will go into effect starting January 2014, once the current program ends.\par \par \uc2 While the market had anticipated asset purchases, "it's the timing" that appeared to support the strengthening in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Dean Popplewell, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at trading platform Oanda.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are disappointed that the asset purchasing will predominantly take place in 2014, which is much further along the curve than people had anticipated," he said, adding that the market had expected "a bit more urgency" from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Abe's recently installed government.\par \par \uc2 The ICE dollar index (DXY), which measures the greenback against a basket of six major global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dropped to 79.870 from 80.046 late Monday. The WSJ Dollar Index , which uses a slightly wider basket, also fell 0.3% to 70.73.\par \par \uc2 Yen's room to run?\par \par \uc2 The dollar/yen pair could be pushed lower toward the Yen86.50 to Yen87 level, giving the market a chance to test that support range and "see what demand there is for U.S. dollars down there," said Popplewell. But as of now, the market's opted to "buy back some of their short yen positions they've been accumulating over the last three months or so."\par \par \uc2 Analysts at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  told clients if the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  begins to appreciate, "we are certain that we will see new measures from [the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 ] and the government. Hence, we still forecast that both EUR/JPY and USD/JPY will move higher in 2013, but the pace will most likely slow now."\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, analysts at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be in a "compromise formation" in light of its latest moves, which can hardly be seen as aggressive.\par \par \uc2 "A more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could cut interest on current deposit account at the BOJ and purchasing foreign bonds, for example, will likely await the new leadership that should be in place in the April-May period," they said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar largely held steady after an industry report showed U.S. sales of existing homes edged down by 1% in December, while the 2012 total reached its highest level in five years.\par \par \uc2 German investor sentiment rises\par \par \uc2 Within other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crosses, the euro (EURUSD) was largely steady at $1.3311 versus $1.3312 in late trading on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Underpinning the euro, the German ZEW economic-expectations index, a gauge of investor sentiment, rose more sharply than anticipated in January. The indicator for economic sentiment in the country rose to the highest level since May 2010.\par \par \uc2 "It is important because it lends credence to the Bundesbank's optimism that after contracting in Q4 (by as much as 0.5% q/q), the euro area's largest economy was already recovering," said analysts at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 . "Attention now shifts to Thursday's flash PMI readings for further confirmation."\par \par \uc2 The analysts said speculation of a resignation by Bundesbank President Jans Weidmann, which they noted was denied by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and rumors of a large loss at a German bank had weighed on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier.\par \par \uc2 Weidmann warned in a speech a day earlier that central banks were in danger of losing their independence. In loosely translated remarks, he said attacks on independence by those banks can already be seen in Hungary or \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  "where the new government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the affairs of" central banks.\par \par \uc2 One consequence, he said, is an increasing politicization of the exchange rate. "So far, the international monetary system came without competitive devaluations by the crisis and I hope it stays," he said.\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires  }}}\uc2  [ 01-22-13 1509ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020130122e91m00073\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
