\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Japan Econ Min: Govt, BOJ Must Show Markets Will To Overcome Deflation\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Dezember 2012\par 12:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Important for the government and BOJ to show the market their intention to work together, Japan economy minister says\par \par \uc2 --He says appropriate candidate for next BOJ governor could come from MOF\par \par \uc2 --Japan's participation in TPP negotiations difficult if current conditions don't change, he also says\par \par \uc2 (Adds background throughout, quotes in 7th, 9th, 12-13th paragraphs.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eleanor Warnock \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--Japan's new economy minister said Friday that the government needs to show its strong intention to get the nation's moribund economy back on track and end 15 years of deflation, but remained firm about the need to consider many policy options.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Akira Amari is charged with crafting economic growth strategies for the new government as well as leading discussions about economic and monetary policy in a government council that the Bank of Japan governor would also attend.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's important for the government and the BOJ to express clearly to markets their cooperation and strong intentions" towards achieving a 2% inflation target, he said during a group press conference.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition to economic stimulus to boost growth, the new Liberal Democratic Party-led administration and its leader, Shinzo Abe, have said a more accommodative Bank of Japan is also necessary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In February, the BOJ set a "goal" for the first time to achieve a price rise of 1% in the near term. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decided to review the goal this month, partly in response to political pressure.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market focus is also on who will be appointed the next BOJ governor when the current head Masaaki Shirakawa's tenure expires in April.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If that person thinks not just in the interest of his ministry, but of his country, someone from any ministry is alright," including someone from the finance ministry, Mr. Amari said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in charge of state finances and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  affairs, such an appointment could be seen as a conflict of interest that compromises the bank's independence from the government.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chief Cabinet Secretary Yoshihide Suga said earlier Friday that the government was considering starting a foreign-bond buying fund to help overcome deflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If a private fund buys, then it's investing, but depending on how much the government is involved, it can be judged as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and not investment," Mr. Amari said, adding that the government should exercise caution about such a fund's effects on the target of its buying and consider options, including involving the private sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Because Japan would have to sell the yen to buy foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in order to purchase a target country's bonds, weakening the yen, such a move could be considered a form of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  has criticized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  before for unilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As part of its campaign promises, the LDP said it would be opposed to participating in negotiations for the Trans-Pacific Partnership free-trade agreement if unconditional tariff elimination was necessary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Though Mr. Amari said that "it would be difficult for the Abe administration to enter (negotiations) if the situation did not change," he also raised the issue of what the agreement would look like without Japan's participation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The U.S. is trying to build a bridge to East Asia with the TPP," he said. "A TPP without Japan will not be a bridge to East Asia. It's up to the U.S. to understand that."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Eleanor Warnock at eleanor.warnock@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 28, 2012 06:04 ET (11:04 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121228e8cs00235\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
