\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Japan Fin Min Jojima: Econ Conditions Getting More Difficult\b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2012\par 06:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:16 EDT *DJ  Japan Fin Min Jojima: Recognize Recession Is A Possibility\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:29 EDT *DJ  Japan Fin Min Jojima: Strong Yen Reflects Structural Factors Such As Global Econ Slump, Europe Debt Crisis\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:33 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fin Min Jojima: Keep \b \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  In Mind In Times Of Excess Volatility\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:39 EDT *DJ  Japan Fin Min Jojima: Keeping Sense Of Tension On \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market, To Respond Appropriately\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:40 EDT *DJ  Japan Fin Min Jojima: Maintaining Strong Sense Of Caution In Dealing With Strong Yen\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:54 EDT *DJ  Japan Fin Min Jojima: Continue To Expect Powerful Easing By BOJ\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 00:58 EDT *DJ  Japan Jojima: Strongly Expect BOJ To Do Its Part To Achieve 1% Inflation Goal\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 01:00 EDT *DJ  Japan Jojima: Greater Govt Involvement In BOJ Affairs Needs To Be Considered With Caution\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 01:00 EDT *DJ  Japan Jojima: BOJ Has Handled Monetary Policy Appropriately\par \par \uc2 7 Nov 2012 01:53 EDT DJ  Japan Fin Min Jojima: Maintaining Strong Sense of Alert in Dealing With Strong Yen\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Mitsuru Obe \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--Japanese finance minister Koriki Jojima emphasized his strong determination to deal with the strong yen Wednesday, saying he is looking at the unit's export-crippling strength with a sense of elevated caution.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I am handling the issue of the strong yen with a strong sense of alert," he said during a parliamentary committee meeting. He said he is "closely watching" the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and intends to "respond appropriately."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Jojima reiterated a joint commitment by the government and the Bank of Japan to cooperate to overcome deflation. "I have strong expectations the BOJ will play a part in achieving the goal of 1% inflation," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Jojima refrained from placing the blame for the nation's persistent deflation on the BOJ, saying "the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been handling monetary policy appropriately."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The government is prepared to do its part" in dealing with deflation, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Mitsuru Obe at mitsuru.obe@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8 Nov 2012 18:51 EDT *DJ \par Japan Fin Min Jojima: Need To Closely Watch Direction Of Current Account Balance\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8 Nov 2012 18:52 EDT *DJ \par Japan Fin Min Jojima: Sept Current Account Deficit Due Mainly To Large Fuel Imports\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8 Nov 2012 18:55 EDT *DJ \par Japan Fin Min Jojima: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oil Price, Overseas Econs Will Likely Influence Current Account\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 8 Nov 2012 19:16 EDT DJ \par Japan Fin Min Jojima: Need To Closely Watch Direction Of Current Account\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Mitsuru Obe\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--Japan's finance minister said Friday that the direction of the nation's current account balance should be closely watched, following a drop into deficit in September on a seasonally adjusted basis for the first time in more than 30 years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The direction (of the current account) will need to be monitored closely," Finance Minister Koriki Jojima said in a regular press conference.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Jojima said a surge in imports of fossil fuels was the main cause of the deficit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the outlook for the current account balance, he said: "It is difficult to predict one way or another," noting it would be influenced by external factors such as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate, crude oil prices, and overseas economic conditions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The current account measures trade in goods, services and investments with the rest of the world.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Mitsuru Obe at mitsuru.obe@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 08, 2012 19:16 ET (00:16 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121107e8b7001hr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
