\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ UPDATE: HKMA Moves to Weaken  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  for First Time in Three Years\b0\par\par\uc2 By Fiona Law   \par \uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2012\par 16:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--After weeks of capital inflows from abroad that have pushed up the value of the Hong Kong dollar to the top of its trading band, the city's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday and weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in nearly three years.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's latest round of stimulus measures and the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent pledge to buy sovereign bonds has restored global investor confidence and led money managers to buy a wide range of assets around the world.\par \par \uc2 The influx of money has also pushed up the Hang Seng Index--the benchmark of local shares that's closely tied to the fortunes of China--to a six-month high, making it one of Asia's best performers in 2012.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 4.67 billion Hong Kong dollars (US$603 million) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday during New York trading as the U.S. dollar hit HK$7.7500, the upper limit of where the Hong Kong dollar is allowed to trade against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The move on Friday was small and well expected by traders given the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trading around HK$7.76 for weeks. The HKMA undertakes to buy or sell the local unit whenever it touches either side of the band that ranges from HK$7.75 to HK$7.85.\par \par \uc2 Still, this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was different from the last time Hong Kong stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the height of the financial crisis. From October 2008 to December 2009, the HKMA repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame the Hong Kong dollar, as the tightly controlled dollar-pegged local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen as a safe-haven asset amid global market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 An HKMA spokeswoman, who declined to be named, said Saturday there had been robust demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently, driven by a stabilized European market and a weak greenback.\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this time around also comes as other central banks in region also seek to stop their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening further to help keep their exports competitively priced. The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the yen's appreciation while \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  is suspected of curbing the won's rally.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is also partly seen as a proxy for China's yuan, also called the renminbi, which is trading near a 19-year high against the U.S. dollar, but isn't fully convertible so difficult for foreign investors to buy.\par \par \uc2 "Capital inflow to Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue, at least, through the end of this year, should the greenback remain weak ahead of the U.S. presidential election in November. The Hong Kong dollar will be one of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain bolstered, as it's more liquid, and the renminbi is strengthening," said Woody Chan, treasurer of Citic Bank Corp.'s Hong Kong unit. "Further invention from the HKMA could be seen in the near future."\par \par \uc2 Hong Kong's linked exchange-rate regime was established in 1983, partly to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from panic selling amid escalating concerns on the former British colony's future, ahead of its handover to China in 1997.\par \par \uc2 The peg bolts Hong Kong's monetary policy to that of the U.S., meaning the city has had ultralow interest rates recently, spurring rising property prices because money is cheap to borrow for real estate purchases.\par \par \uc2 That's led to calls for a review of the system, including from the former head of the HKMA, Joseph Yam, who said in a research paper earlier this year that it was time for the government to look at options including a switch to pegging to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a complete float.\par \par \uc2 "The re-appreciation in the renminbi has given the Hong Kong dollar a further boost and led to some speculation on the dollar peg regime," said \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2  senior strategist Frances Cheung.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA says it has no intention to change the linked exchange rate system, citing it as an anchor of Hong Kong's financial and economic stability.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Fiona Law at fiona.law@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020121021e8al0012x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
