\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.COM Worldwide News Briefs\b0\par\par\uc2 1,161 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2012\par 23:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPAIN DEFIES DOWNGRADES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish officials said they were caught off guard by a credit downgrade that left the country teetering a notch above junk status at two of the three main rating firms, but said the move was unjustified and wouldn't affect their plans to raise money on financial markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LAGARDE URGES MORE TIME FOR GREECE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde said Greece should be given an extra two years to meet its budget targets, publicly wading into the politically sensitive bailout discussions under way.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREECE'S STATE BUDGET GAP NARROWS SHARPLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's state budget deficit narrowed sharply in the first nine months of 2012, beating targets set by the country's creditors despite revenue collection falling short of expectations due to the recession and strike by tax collectors.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EGYPT'S PRESIDENT OUSTS TOP PROSECUTOR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Egypt's president removed his prosecutor general after a court-ordered acquittal of 24 loyalists of ousted President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hosni Mubarak\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. NAMES NEW TOP DIPLOMAT FOR LIBYA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Obama administration named a new top diplomat for Libya on Thursday to take the place of Christopher Stevens, the U.S. ambassador who was killed in last month's assault on the U.S. consulate in Benghazi.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI COURT ISSUES WARRANT FOR THAKSIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Thai leader \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thaksin Shinawatra\f28 \uc2 \f2  faces more legal difficulties after the Supreme Court issued an arrest warrant in connection with a case involving nearly $390 million in loans extended by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GLOOM GOES GLOBAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weakness in major economies is starting to infect formerly fast-growing emerging markets, top global economic officials warned, raising fears of a prolonged world-wide slowdown.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. DRONE KILLS 16 IN PAKISTAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. drones fired missiles in a Pakistani tribal region, killing 16 militants, while bombings elsewhere killed 10 civilians and three security personnel, officials said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TURKEY REINS IN CURRENT-ACCOUNT DEFICIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkey's current-account deficit shrank more than forecast to its narrowest in almost three years, increasing the nation's chances of winning investment-grade status from credit rating companies\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. SECURITY CUT BEFORE LIBYA RAID \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The State Department cut U.S. security staff in Libya before the Benghazi attack despite requests for more personnel, two former officials testified.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. WINDS DOWN AFGHAN AID PROGRAM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. military is ending a massive nation-building experiment in Afghanistan, shutting down teams that have poured hundreds of millions of dollars into roads, schools and administrative buildings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SOUTH AFRICA MINERS REJECT PAY OFFER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Talks broke down between mine companies and unions representing some 50,000 workers on strike at South Africa's three top gold producers.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ON YEN WITHOUT U.S. SUPPORT \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economy minister, Seiji Maehara, said Tokyo may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein in the yen's strength, even without the consent of the U.S., and that the countries' differences on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  couldn't be resolved through negotiations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ MINUTES, WEAK DATA RAISE EASING PROSPECTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September minutes from Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and weak August data on machinery orders raise prospects of fresh BOJ steps later this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN TO RESUME AID TO MYANMAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan announced a plan to restart yen loans to Myanmar, as Tokyo steps up efforts to help bring the once-pariah Southeast Asian nation into the fold of the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CREDITORS AGREE TO SUPPORT MYANMAR CHANGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A meeting of Myanmar's key international creditors agreed on the importance of supporting the country's reforms, though they didn't reach a comprehensive deal to reduce the enation's debt burden.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SHELL FACES OIL-SPILL CLAIMS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Royal Dutch Shell\f28 \uc2 \f2  appeared in court in the Netherlands for the first time over the actions of one of its foreign subsidiaries, facing compensation claims for environmental damage from oil spills in Nigeria.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par POLICE ARREST DELHI ATTACK SUSPECTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian police have arrested three Muslim militants suspected of planning terror attacks in New Delhi during a major Hindu festival season that starts later this month, a top police official said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S GILLARD RECLAIMS SPOTLIGHT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prime Minister Julia Gillard's 15-minute verbal attack on opposition leader Tony Abbott-accusing him of sexism and misogyny- has gone viral and fueled debate about gender bias in politics.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CZECH RIGHT FACES LOSSES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The center-right national government is expected to take a drubbing in regional and senatorial elections this weekend as voters kick back against austerity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LONDON OLYMPICS FAIL TO BOOST SPENDING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The London 2012 Olympic and Paralympic Games failed to provide a boost to spending from visiting tourists over the summer, while the number of overseas visitors to the U.K. was lower than a year earlier.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FEARS OF NEW BALI THREAT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesian authorities warned that terrorist groups may be planning an attack targeting dignitaries and events in Bali this week to commemorate the 10th anniversary of the deadly attacks on the resort island in 2002.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NETANYAHU'S COALITION SEEN AS A CRUCIAL QUESTION IN ELECTION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Netanyahu is widely expected to win re-election with a campaign focused on national security. However, the vote will be far from meaningless because the election has the potential to spur a makeover of Mr. Netanyahu's coalition.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU TO PRESS FOR UNIFIED AIRSPACE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European Union Transport Commissioner Siim Kallas is preparing legal action against EU member countries to force faster action on a delayed program to unify the bloc's airspace, according to a speech he will deliver Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA'S BUREAUCRACY SLOWS TUBERCULOSIS TREATMENT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rahima Sheikh, a TB patient carrying a nearly untreatable strain of the disease, is perilously close to running out of the medicines that appear to be saving her life.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADIAN OFFICER PLEADS GUILTY TO LEAKING DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Canadian naval officer pleaded guilty to leaking military-communications intelligence in a case that has embarrassed the country's military.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CH\u193\'00\'C1VEZ TAPS HIS POSSIBLE SUCCESSOR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hugo Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez\f28 \uc2 \f2  named his foreign minister, who is a former bus driver and union activist, as his next vice president-and potential successor-after the Venezuelan leader won his re-election.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RUSSIA TO END ARMS-DISPOSAL DEAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia said it won't renew a U.S.-funded arms-disposal agreement that has helped Moscow safeguard and destroy thousands of nuclear warheads and chemical weapons since the collapse of the Soviet Union.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH POLICE FIND BOMB-MAKING MATERIALS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French authorities extended the custody of 12 members of an alleged homegrown terror cell for an extra day without charges, following the discovery of a storage unit used by one suspect that contained weapons.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BULLET REMOVED FROM PAKISTANI GIRL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pakistani doctors successfully removed a bullet from the neck of a 14-year-old girl who was shot by the Taliban for speaking out in support of education for women.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YEMEN DETAINS U.S. CITIZEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yemen's security forces detained a U.S. citizen suspected of having links to al Qaeda, a Yemeni official said Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .) [ 10-11-12 1700ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020121011e8ab000sx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwg