\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 28\b0\par\par\uc2 1,564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2012\par 08:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: WEAK JAPANESE ECONOMIC DATA SHOWS GROWING RISK OF RECESSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Weak economic data released by the government Friday showed that the Japanese economy may be slowing more than expected amid headwinds from overseas, and could possibly move into a recession. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FITCH: CHINA, INDIA LIKELY TO EXPAND AT SLOWER PACE THAN EXPECTED IN 2012 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China and India's economies are likely to expand at a slower pace this year than previously expected, amid worsening prospects for global growth and reduced ability or willingness in the two countries to implement policy stimulus, Fitch Ratings said Friday. (published 0148 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA OUTPUT FALLS FOR 3RD STRAIGHT MONTH IN AUG; PAVES WAY FOR RATE CUT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's factory output fell for a third consecutive month in August as strikes in the automobile sector and two typhoons slowed business activities, paving the way for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to deliver another policy rate cut. (published 0210 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA CURRENT-ACCOUNT SURPLUS AT 4-MONTH LOW AS EXTERNAL WOE WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's current-account surplus fell to a four-month low in August from a record-high in July as weak export demand combined with seasonal factors, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO PRODUCTION UP 4.5% ON YEAR IN AUG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Production of cars, trucks and buses in Japan increased 4.5% on year in August, rising for the 11th consecutive month, as the government's buying incentives spurred demand of fuel-efficient vehicles. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S AUTO EXPORTS FALL 5.4% ON YEAR IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports of cars, trucks and buses declined 5.4% on year in August, falling for the first time in eight months, as the stubbornly strong yen makes it hard to export vehicles profitably. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WEAK AUSTRALIA CREDIT GROWTH FUELS RATE CUT CALLS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia recorded only a slight increase in credit growth in August from July, supporting calls for a cut in interest rates when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy-making board next meets on Tuesday, according to economists. (published 0317 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER WANTS SUCCESSOR TO CONVEY YEN WORRIES DURING IMF, \f28 \uc2 \f2 G-7\f28 \uc2 \f2  MEETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's outgoing finance minister said Friday he wants his successor to convey Tokyo's concerns over the yen's persistent strength during the upcoming \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  meetings, suggesting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's efforts to win support for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MOODY'S DOWNGRADES VIETNAM ON BANK-RELATED WEAKNESSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service Friday cut Vietnam's credit rating to B2 from B1, citing risks that the government will have to pump money into the country's banking system, and the latter's limited ability to support the economy. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI AUG INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION INDEX FALLS 11.32% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial production index fell in August for a third straight month, the Ministry of Industry's Office of Industrial Economics said in a statement Friday. (published 0325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI MINISTRY: LIKELY TO TRIM 2012 INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION GROWTH TARGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's Ministry of Industry said Friday that it is likely to trim its target for 2012 industrial production growth of 6%-7% after industrial output dropped by 5.37% during the first eight months of the year. (published 0502 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA TRADE DEFICIT LIKELY NARROWED IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia likely posted a trade deficit for the fifth consecutive month in August on weak demand from main export markets and a further dip in some commodities prices, though the deficit was likely to have narrowed from the preceding month. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA SEPTEMBER CPI LIKELY +4.60% ON YEAR, +0.26% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer prices in Indonesia likely rose at a slightly faster pace in September from a year earlier as food prices remained elevated due to a drought in the U.S., but most economists think this won't lead the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to raise rates as inflation is still within its target range. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FRASER & NEAVE\f28 \uc2 \f2  SHAREHOLDERS BACK \f28 \uc2 \f2 HEINEKEN\f28 \uc2 \f2 'S BID FOR ASIA PACIFIC BREWERIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shareholders of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fraser & Neave Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday agreed to sell their stake in a beer joint venture to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Heineken N.V\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for about $4.6 billion, ending a two-month saga in which the Dutch brewer's bid to strengthen its foothold in the lucrative Asian beer market looked to be threatened by a reclusive Thai billionaire. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SHARP SECURES Y360B LOAN DEAL WITH BANKS AMID HON HAI IMPASSE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sharp Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has reached a deal to receive a 360 billion yen syndicated loan, helping keep the struggling electronics maker's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  afloat amid an apparent standstill in talks with Taiwan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hon Hai Precision Industry Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . over a previously agreed capital injection. (published 0116 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASTRO MALAYSIA INSTITUTIONAL TRANCHE OF IPO MORE THAN 20 TIMES COVERED -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian cable television operator Astro Malaysia Holdings Bhd.'s up to $1.5 billion initial public offering has attracted bids totaling more than 20 times the amount of shares available for institutional investors, two people familiar with the deal said Friday. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AIR NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO UNDERTAKE SHARE BUYBACK FOR UP TO 3% OF COMPANY'S SHARES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it would undertake an on-market share buyback program for up to 3% of its shares and said it is on track to double its normalized earnings before taxation in the current financial year. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TELECOM CORP. OF NEW ZEALAND\f28 \uc2 \f2  REITERATES TEPID FISCAL 2013 OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON, New Zealand--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Telecom Corp. of New Zealand Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reiterated Friday its expectation for little growth in its operating profit this year. (published 2236 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WOOLWORTHS SAYS CHAIRMAN, STRONG, SET TO RETIRE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 James Strong\f28 \uc2 \f2  would retire after the company's annual general meeting in November. (published 0002 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ UPDATE: RESEARCH IN MOTION POSTS SMALLER 2ND-QUARTER LOSS THAN EXPECTED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Research In Motion Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . posted its third straight quarterly loss in the period ended Sept. 1, but its revenue and operating loss came in significantly better than expected, and it actually increased its subscriber base and cash position. (published 2237 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 NIKE\f28 \uc2 \f2  PROFIT FALLS 12% ON OVERHEAD COSTS, SLOWER CHINA GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nike Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported its second-straight quarter of declining profit Thursday, with fiscal first-quarter earnings falling 12% as slowed growth in China and a surge in marketing costs weighed on its bottom line. (published 2310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: MICRON 4TH-QUARTER LOSS WIDENS ON SALES DECLINES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Micron Technology Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported its fifth-straight quarterly loss as weak demand for memory used in servers and personal computers continued to drag down revenue. (published 2251 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: AMAZON PLANNING ONLINE WINE SALES - WINERIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Amazon.com Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is planning an online marketplace for wine sales directly to consumers, said executives for several California wineries, marking the Seattle Web giant's second foray into the business in three years. (published 0134 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES HIGHER AT QUARTER-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian markets were higher Friday at the end of the third quarter, as Chinese stocks continued to push away from lows touched earlier this week, while Japan was weighed down by weak industrial data. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: THAI JASMINE RICE OUTPUT SUFFERS ON DRY WEATHER; VIETNAM TO GAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BALI, Indonesia--Thailand's exports of premium fragrant Jasmine rice, already down due to high prices and tight supply sparked by a government buying program, will take a further hit when the new crop is harvested because of dry weather in several growing regions in August, a top exporter said Friday. (published 0353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAKISTAN 2013 RICE EXPORTS TO CHINA TO DOUBLE TO 700,000 TONS -EXECUTIVE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BALI, Indonesia--Pakistan's 2013 rice exports to China are expected to double to 700,000 metric tons due to strong demand and limited availability of rice from Thailand, a leading Karachi-based exporter said Friday. (published 0455 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM EXPORTERS IN TALKS WITH INDONESIA TO SELL RICE - EXECUTIVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BALI, Indonesia--Vietnamese rice exporters are in talks with Indonesia's state-run procurement agency Bulog to sell rice for shipment in the next few months, trading executives said Friday. (published 0014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM GOVERNMENT: TO HALVE COAL EXPORT TAX TO 10% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's government has decided to lower its export tax on coal to 10% from 20% to improve competitiveness, the government said in a statement late Thursday, without saying when the new rate will take effect. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SELLS 400,010 TONS SOYBEANS FROM STATE RESERVES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China sold all 400,010 metric tons of state-reserve soybeans that it offered in an auction Thursday, with the average price falling from a record set two weeks ago, the state-backed China National Grain & Oils Information Center said Friday. (published 0218 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SRI LANKA TARGETING SUGAR SELF-SUFFICIENCY BY 2019 -MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sri Lanka is targeting sugar self-sufficiency by 2019, Laisshman Senewiratne, minister of productivity promotion, said Friday. (published 0358 GMT) [ 28-09-12 0607GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120928e89s0008n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
