\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Steadies After Overnight Falls\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2012\par 07:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Euro steadies after overnight falls on weak German Ifo, Spain concerns\par \par \uc2 --Focus on Merkel-Draghi meeting, Spanish bail-out\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Alexander Martin \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro steadied during Asian trading Tuesday after its overnight fall on weak Germon Ifo sentiment data and concerns about a potential Spanish bailout.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany's Ifo Institute's business sentiment indicator fell for a fifth straight month, casting doubts on the strength of the euro zone's largest economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spain's reluctance to officially ask for an international bailout has also been weighing on investor sentiment. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said earlier this month that it would buy unlimited amounts of short-dated bonds from countries that ask for financial help and comply with any conditions attached.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "With Spain indecisive on the bail-out issue, risk sentiment is mixed," said Junichi Ishikawa, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at IG Market Securities in Tokyo, adding that the dollar was being sold as investors adjust their positions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market will be watching German Chancellor Angela Merkel's meeting with European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  later today.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Ishikawa said focus was on Europe this week as Spain is expected to unveil its draft budget plan for 2013, while a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  credit review of Spain is also expected.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile the dollar remained below Y78.00 after yen-crosses were sold on concerns over the European financial crisis, according to dealers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Osao Iizuka, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said trading was likely to be dominated by commercial flows ahead of firms' half-year book closing at the end of this month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Trading could be range-bound, but once the pair falls below recent low of 77.13, caution (over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) should grow," Iizuka adds.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Tuesday that he will continue to deal with speculative moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market until he leaves his post following a Cabinet reshuffle.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You shouldn't assume any policy gap will be created" by the change in position, said Jun Azumi.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the euro was at $1.2938 from $1.2930 late New York trading Monday, according to trading platform EBS. The common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at Y100.63 from Y100.62 while the dollar was at Y77.77 from Y77.83.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 69.446 from 69.479.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            77.75-78       77.83-87  -0.11    77.92    77.76  +1.11 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2936-40      1.2929-33  +0.05   1.2953   1.2930  -0.17 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.6225-30      1.6217-21  +0.05   1.6236   1.6218  +4.41 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9352-56      0.9356-61  -0.05   0.9362   0.9344  -0.20 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9791-96      0.9783-87  +0.09   0.9795   0.9782  -4.08 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0430-34      1.0423-27  +0.07   1.0444   1.0418  +2.19 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8230-36      0.8227-32  +0.04   0.8242   0.8212  +5.88 \par  \par Euro Rate \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan           100.61-64      100.64-75  -0.07   100.83   100.62  +1.07 \par  \par Source: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICAP PLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Alexander Martin at alexander.martin@dowjones.com [ 25-09-12 0513GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120925e89p00065\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
