\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro falls to more than one-week low vs dollar, yen\b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2012\par 20:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds quotes, changes byline)\par \par \uc2 * Euro falls after German Ifo disappoints\par \par \uc2 * Uncertainty on Spain, Greece also undermines euro\par \par \uc2 * BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on radar as dollar falls versus yen\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 24 (Reuters) - The euro fell to its lowest in more than a week against the dollar and yen on Monday as a weak German business sentiment report and uncertainty about debt-plagued Spain added to concerns about the euro zone's slumping economy.\par \par \uc2 The drop in German business sentiment in September to its lowest since early 2010 raised worries that Germany, the largest euro zone economy, is succumbing to a downturn despite the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recently announced bond-buying plan.\par \par \uc2 Spain is also adding to the euro zone's pain. Spanish government bond yields rose on signs Madrid is making slow progress toward asking for the international bailout that markets are anticipating. Italian yields also rose.\par \par \uc2 Many market participants also believe the euro is poised for a pullback after a sharp rally in recent weeks that took the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a four-month high against the dollar at $1.3169 on Sept. 17.\par \par \uc2 Data on Friday from the U.S. derivatives watchdog CFTC showed speculators' net euro short positions shrank to their lowest since November, having fallen to just above one-third of the record peak reached in June.\par \par \uc2 "We seem to have reached a top in the euro. Things are still problematic in the euro zone," said Matthew Lifson, senior trader and analyst at Cambridge Mercantile Group in Princeton, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 The euro hit a session low of $1.2889, its lowest since Sept. 13. It last traded at $1.2921, down 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Initial support is seen at $1.2905, the 23.6 percent retracement of the July to September rally, followed by its 200-day moving average, which comes in around $1.2828.\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the euro last traded at 100.54 yen , down 0.8 percent. It dropped to 100.33, a more than one-week low.\par \par \uc2 The Munich-based Ifo think tank said its business climate index, based on a monthly survey of some 7,000 firms, fell to 101.4 in September from 102.3 in August. A Reuters poll of 45 economists had forecast a slight rise to 102.5.\par \par \uc2 In the last few weeks, the euro has benefited from the dollar's weakness following the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's announcement of another round of monetary stimulus to boost the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 That rally in the euro seemed to have run out of steam.\par \par \uc2 "The initial investor enthusiasm following ... the Fed QE3 (quantitative easing) announcement has begun to wane as the more intractable problems of the euro zone sovereign debt crisis return to the front burner," said Samarjit Shankar, managing director for global strategy at \uc2 BNY Mellon\uc2  in Boston.\par \par \uc2 SPANISH BUDGET\par \par \uc2 Madrid is expected to present its draft budget plan for 2013 this week and announce new structural reforms, while the results of stress tests on the wobbly Spanish banking sector are also due. These could set the stage for a full-scale bailout.\par \par \uc2 However, Economy Minister Luis de Guindos said on Saturday Spain will not rush to seek external aid to finance its debt, and EU officials said they did not expect Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy to seek an assistance program before a regional election in his native Galicia on Oct. 21.\par \par \uc2 Adding to pressure for Spain is the risk of a downgrade of its sovereign debt rating to junk status by ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2 , which some expect this week, as well as a 27.5 billion euro refinancing hump at the end of next month.\par \par \uc2 Further weighing on the euro was a possible delay in the release of an EU/IMF report on whether Greece's debt is manageable. That report, now expected to be released until after Nov. 6, was originally expected next month.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell against the yen, trading at 77.86 yen , down 0.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Risk aversion firmly favored the yen but \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market should the yen gain further, traders said. The Bank of Japan's easing last week is seen as paving the way for such a move.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Julie Haviv; Editing by James Dalgleish)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 7) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | AUF | CANT | J | RBN | ABX | BNX | FUN | UKI | Z | RNP | DNP | PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120924e89o00127\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
