\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Higher As Sentiment Still Upbeat On Fed Action\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2012\par 08:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Yen also gains slightly against the dollar, raising \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears\par \par \uc2 --More dollar weakness in store in the near-term, says RBS\par \par \uc2 --Korean won reaches six-month high\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Martin Vaughan \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE--The euro gained modestly in Asia Monday as investors remained upbeat following last week's announcement by the U.S. Federal Reserve that it would buy more bonds, but the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traded well below its Friday peak.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen also strengthened against the U.S. unit, though trade was thin because Tokyo markets were closed for a holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The euro is probably pausing here for breath, and may backfill a little," said RBS senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Greg Gibbs. "But the market still anticipates the Fed expanding its balance sheet over the next several months, and that will continue to weigh on the U.S. dollar."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0615 GMT the euro was trading at $1.3133 according to EBS via CQG, compared with $1.3127 late Friday in New York. The euro on Friday was as high as $1.3166, a four-month peak.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday the dollar slid against the yen, which could renew expectations that Japanese authorities would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow the strengthening \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . For now investors, who pushed up the dollar on Friday, seemed willing to "front run \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to save them the bother," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Sean Callow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Callow said he expected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to refrain from any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy meeting Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were mixed Monday. The dollar hit a fresh six-month low against the Korean won at KRW1,114.70 as foreign investors bought up Korean equities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Singapore dollar, meanwhile, weakened against the U.S. unit following a sharper-than expected drop in August exports. That is feeding expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore will ease up on its strong-Singapore dollar stance at its October policy meeting, which could in turn lead to some unwinding of bullish Singapore-dollar positions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile the Australian dollar slipped against the greenback to trade at $1.0536 at 0615 GMT, down from $1.0552 late Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            78.30-34       78.34-38  -0.05    78.47    78.18  +1.83 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.3129-32      1.3120-24  +0.06   1.3140   1.3106  +1.31 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.6223-26      1.6219-24  +0.02   1.6236   1.6214  +4.39 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9254-58      0.9260-71  -0.11   0.9275   0.9250  -1.24 \par USD/CAD Canada          0.9693-98     0.9697-706  -0.06   0.9719   0.9694  -5.04 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0531-42      1.0552-57  -0.17   1.0556   1.0518  +3.21 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8284-88     0.8293-300  -0.13   0.8302   0.8276  +6.56 \par  \par Euro Rate \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan           102.83-86      102.83-90  -0.02   102.93   102.64  +3.30 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Martin Vaughan at martin.vaughan@dowjones.com [ 17-09-12 0635GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120917e89h0009a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
