\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Powers Ahead After Fed Ushers in QE3\b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2012\par 13:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Euro at four-month highs against dollar and yen\par \par \uc2 -- Dollar recovers against yen amid \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  chatter\par \par \uc2 -- Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also higher\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Eva Szalay \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro rose to another four-month high against the dollar Friday and notched up strong gains against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  pulled the trigger on a fresh stimulus package for the U.S. economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The single European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended its overnight push above $1.30 against the greenback and powered to a near four-month high against the Japanese yen above Y102 as relatively safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under selling pressure in the wake of the Fed's announcement late Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would keep interest rates near zero until mid-2015 and undertake more asset purchases where necessary, to encourage more investment in the flagging U.S. economy and jobs market, prompting analysts to predict further weakness in the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There remains plenty of scope for investors to increase the use of the dollar as a funding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following the commitment to loose policy from the Fed," said Michael Sneyd, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar also plumbed four-month lows against sterling and the Swiss franc, but did at least make gains against the yen, firming above Y78 after initially dropping to its weakest level since February in the immediate aftermath of the Fed statement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bounce in the dollar against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  occurred after traders reported that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had checked market rates ahead of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to counter yen strength and amid talk of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy action in the coming days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Expectations are building for more monetary easing measures from the BOJ to be announced at its meeting next week," said Lee Hardman, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi-UFJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  in London.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling was a beneficiary of the losses in the dollar and the yen, trading as high as $1.6243 and Y126.93, its highest levels since May.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also got a boost, with the Polish zloty inching toward its strongest level of the year against the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while the Hungarian forint also saw heavy gains. Selling pressure on the South African rand abated somewhat, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sank to its lowest level against the euro late Thursday and remained week in European hours Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1048 GMT, the euro traded at $1.3094 compared with $1.2987 late Thursday in New York, according to EBS via CQG. Against the yen, the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was at Y102.17 from Y100.68 the previous day, and the dollar was at Y78.04 compared with Y77.48.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at about 68.938 from 69.192.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A summary of key levels for chart-watching technical strategists is below:\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1032 GMT     1.3088     78.02      1.6239     0.9302 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish    Bullish    Bullish    Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bullish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.2838     79.22      1.5777     0.9415 \par 3rd Resistance    1.3284     78.85      1.6453     0.9435 \par 2nd Resistance    1.3179     78.33      1.6360     0.9408 \par 1st Resistance    1.3093     78.24      1.6302     0.9357 \par Pivot*            1.2948     77.49      1.6137     0.9375 \par 1st Support       1.3021     77.67      1.6185     0.9300 \par 2nd Support       1.2970     77.37      1.6125     0.9225 \par 3rd Support       1.2933     77.13      1.6048     0.9184 \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/JPY \par  \par Spot 1032 GMT     102.11 \par 3 Day Trend       Bullish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish \par 200 day ma        101.72 \par 3rd Resistance    104.45 \par 2nd Resistance    103.59 \par 1st Resistance    102.94 \par Pivot*            100.32 \par 1st Support       101.00 \par 2nd Support       100.60 \par 3rd Support        99.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Dow Jones Technical Strategist Francis Bray contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Eva Szalay