\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Weaker After Fed Action\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anusha Shrivastava   \par \uc2 571 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2012\par 00:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar was weaker against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as markets absorbed the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's move to buy more mortgage-backed bonds.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose to a four-month high versus the dollar and market participants expect the rally to continue.\par \par \uc2 "There is some upside for the euro over the next few weeks as the market digests the Fed move," said Aroop Chatterjee, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 That upside is capped by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own bond-buying plans, he added.\par \par \uc2 With the Fed buying $40 billion of bonds every month in an open-ended program, the money supply in the system increases, thereby weakening the dollar. Ratings firm Egan-Jones cut the sovereign debt rating of the United States to AA-minus from AA, citing the Fed's open-ended efforts to ease monetary policy, also referred to as quantitative easing, or QE3.\par \par \uc2 "The Fed's QE3 will stoke the stock market and commodity prices, but in our opinion will hurt the U.S economy and, by extension, credit quality," the firm said Friday. Egan-Jones said QE3 would reduce the value of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The greenback did strengthen against the yen, which fell as it appeared more likely \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yen had risen to a seven-month high against the dollar on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Jun Azumi strongly hinted Friday that market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tackle the strong yen may be imminent and urged the Bank of Japan to act, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength increasingly threatens to worsen the country's economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 The yen traded recently traded at 78.31 to the dollar, from 77.48 Thursday in New York, its strongest close since Feb. 8.\par \par \uc2 Several banks, including \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 , \uc2 UBS\uc2  and \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 , are revising their euro forecasts higher as the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rocketed over 5% in the past two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Late Friday, the euro was at $1.3132 against the dollar versus $1.2987 in New York Thursday, according to EBS via CQG.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at Nomura Securities in New York are ready to fade the current rally in the euro as they believe the upcoming European event risk "is much more two-way" with a question over whether Spain will request aid from the European Union. If it did, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could buy the countries' bonds. Also, the outlook for growth in the periphery is weak, the analysts wrote.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at Y102.90 against the yen, from Y100.68.\par \par \uc2 The dollar could continue to depreciate versus the euro because of the renewed supply of cash in the system due to the Fed's policies, and the emerging markets and so-called commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the Australian dollar would benefit, Mr. Chatterjee said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Australian dollar rose above $1.0615, its highest level since March 20. Late Friday, it was at $1.0548 versus $1.0547 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The pound was at $1.6210, from $1.6152 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 68.980 from 69.201.\par \par \uc2 --Stephen L. Bernard and Nicole Hong contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Anusha Shrivastava at anusha.shrivastava@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020120914e89e00fa1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
