\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Signals Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Now On Table\b0\par\par\uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2012\par 08:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister says he won't rule out any steps vs excessive yen rises\par \par \uc2 --The minister says he can't overlook recent yen rises, which he calls one-sided\par \par \uc2 --The minister says he wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act appropriately at the right time, and to consider government's economic assessment\par \par \uc2 --The remarks are the latest sign Tokyo's patience with the high yen is wearing thin, stoking speculation that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is imminent\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments by Nissan CEO \uc2 Carlos Ghosn\uc2  in 8th, 9th paragraphs)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi and Mitsuru Obe \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister strongly hinted Friday that market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tackle the strong yen may be imminent and urged the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to act at the right time, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength increasingly threatens to worsen the country's economic slowdown.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Jun Azumi's intensifying efforts to talk down the yen come after the dollar hit a fresh seven-month low of Y77.13 in New York overnight, putting additional stress on Japan's struggling manufacturers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Federal Reserve's announcement Thursday of a major new round of monetary easing to juice U.S. growth dealt a blow to the greenback. The dollar stood at around Y77.62 at around 0345 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Azumi said he understood the Fed's "commitment to revitalizing growth," and noted that a U.S. economic rebound would be "desirable for the world economy." But he characterized the yen's recent climb as "one-sided," and "clearly" out of line with Japan's economic situation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This sort of movement is something I can't overlook," Mr. Azumi said. "I will not rule out any measures and I will take decisive steps when it is deemed necessary. This is the stance I will continue to maintain."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economic picture has sharply deteriorated in recent months due to the European debt crisis, a global slowdown and the yen's stubborn strength.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While government spending has propped up domestic economic activity, "there are now downside risks to exports," Mr. Azumi said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (7201.TO) Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Carlos Ghosn\f28 \uc2 \f2  told the Wall Street Journal that the yen's current levels, with the dollar around Y77-Y78, would hurt Japanese exporters and force manufacturers to move production overseas.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "So this level of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to be a major handicap for companies to continue to maintain high level of activities in Japan, we're going to have to shift more production outside the country," the head Japan's second-largest auto maker said in an interview Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The nation's growth rate dropped to an annualized 0.7% in the April-June period from the previous quarter's stellar 5.3% amid continual trade shortfalls. Some economists now foresee contractions in the next two quarters. The government cut its economic assessment for the second straight month in its September report issued earlier in the day, the first back-to-back downgrades since the global financial crisis that began in 2008.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  has indicated sympathy for Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , there remains a question of whether the U.S. and Europe--both needing improved export performance to support growth--would support such action. Mr. Azumi declined to comment on whether he had had any phone conversations with the U.S. authorities following the Fed's action.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ now seems to be coming under pressure to loosen policy further at a planned meeting next Tuesday and Wednesday to moderate the impact of the Fed's action on the dollar-yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I want the BOJ to take appropriate steps at the appropriate time, by taking into consideration the current economic situation and ... the monthly economic assessment" by the government, Mr. Azumi said. He noted that the BOJ had set a 1% inflation goal in February, and said it was important for the BOJ to take "various steps" to achieve that.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chester Dawson contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com and Mitsuru Obe at mitsuru.obe@dowjones.com [ 14-09-12 0622GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120914e89e000aa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
