\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2012\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SIGNALS YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOW ON TABLE \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister strongly hinted Friday that market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to tackle the strong yen may be imminent and urged the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to act at the right time, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength increasingly threatens to worsen the country's economic slowdown. (published 0346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA STATE RESEARCHERS SAY U.S. QE3 NEGATIVE FOR CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese state researchers reacted negatively to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's new mortgage bond buying program, saying it would lead to inflationary pressures in China and do little to help the real U.S. economy. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S&P UPGRADES SOUTH KOREA RATING TO A-PLUS; OUTLOOK STABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Friday raised South Korea's sovereign credit rating by one notch to A-plus from A, joining the other two global credit rating companies in upgrading Asia's fourth-largest economy. (published 0529 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par STANDARD & POOR'S: CHINA FIRMS COULD FACE DETERIORATING FINANCIAL RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese companies could face deteriorating financial risks as growth of the world's second-largest economy slows, according to a study by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HSBC CHINA CEO SAYS STIMULUS WILL HELP STEADY GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC Holdings Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday that the world's second-biggest economy has a number of measures it can use to stimulate growth, and recently-announced infrastructure investments should help promote "moderate" growth in the fourth quarter of this year. (published 0353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FURUKAWA: NECESSARY FOR BOJ TO KEEP EFFECT OF OVERSEAS IN MIND WHEN ACTING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Friday that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  should consider the impact of developments abroad when reaching a decision over policy at its meeting next week. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA NSW TREASURER CONFIRMS CHINA TALKS ON STATE'S BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's interest in Australian state government bonds has extended to New South Wales, with its treasurer Friday confirming he'd held talks with Beijing as part of moves to broaden the state's investor base. (published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TAIWAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : CLOSELY MONITORING MARKETS AFTER FED EASING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is closely monitoring financial markets after the U.S. Federal Reserve overnight unveiled an open-ended bond buying program and planned to extend low interest rates to 2015 to spur the U.S. economy, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Friday. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HKMA CHIEF: QE3 COULD RAISE PROPERTY BUBBLE RISKS IN HONG KONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Norman Chan said Friday the latest U.S. stimulus plan could increase the risk of a property market bubble forming in the city, and added that the de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would take measures to cool local asset markets if necessary. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : FED MOVE TO INCREASE CAPITAL FLOWS TO EMERGING MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More quantitative easing by the U.S. Federal Reserve is likely increase capital flows to emerging markets such as the Philippines, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor said Friday. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES AUGUST TAX COLLECTION UP 10% AT PHP96.76 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bureau of Internal Revenue, the Philippines' main tax agency, said Friday its collection in August rose 10% to 96.76 billion Philippine pesos . (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EXPORT-IMPORT BANK OF CHINA\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SELL CNY12 BLN BONDS WEDNESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to sell 12 billion yuan worth of seven-year bonds on Wednesday, the policy lender said Friday in a statement on Chinabond, an official website for bond issuance. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DUTCH FINANCE MINISTER: GREECE MAY GET MORE TIME FOR BUDGET GOALS, NOT MORE MONEY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece could get some extra time to meet its budget goals but will not receive additional money, Dutch Finance Minister Jan Kees de Jager said Friday. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: SINGAPORE EXPORTS LIKELY CONTRACTED IN AUGUST AS WORLD ECONOMY SLOWED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's exports likely contracted in August as weakness in the global economy hurt demand. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: STERLING'S RUN COMING TO AN END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This may be the point at which the U.K. economy starts to improve. But it may also be the point at which the pound becomes less attractive. (published 0545 GMT) [ 14-09-12 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120914e89e0008u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
