\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Risk Rises, But Not Yet In Red Zone\b0\par\par\uc2 799 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2012\par 09:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders getting back into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mode, but no panic yet\par \par \uc2 --Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost certain to be after FOMC meeting this week\par \par \uc2 --Also likely to come after BOJ policy board meeting next Wednesday\par \par \uc2 --Key level to watch is Y77.65, where BOJ conducted rate check on June 1 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market is again warily eyeing the possibility of Japanese government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market following the yen's recent rise to three-month highs against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But traders say that they are not yet on high alert with almost no chance of action before the U.S. FOMC concludes its meeting on Thursday, and a likely wait until the Bank of Japan policy board meeting ends next Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's orange very close to red, but not really red yet," said a senior dealer with a major Japanese bank in New York.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell to as low as Y77.70 on the EBS trading platform in New York Tuesday. That was the lowest mark since June 1, when the BOJ conducted a rate-check at Y77.65, a call to traders that can immediately precede actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's relentless rise has been a major headache for Japan's exporters, prompting major automakers and others to step up plans to shift production overseas at the expense of direct exports. Exports have been falling as the yen remained strong. They were off 8.1% in July from the same period last year, capping a fall for seven of the previous 12 months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This in turn has hit the labor market and made it more difficult for the economy to overcome deflationary pressures.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last launched \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in October 2011 with a record-sized dollar buying that pushed the greenback up by more than 5% from a post-war low of Y75.31. That was the fourth round since \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  resumed its market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in September 2010 to cap the value of the yen when the dollar fell below the Y83 level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders say expectations that the Fed will give the go-ahead for another round of quantitative easing at its two-day meeting. Since additional easing would increase the already heavy supply of dollars on the market, the expectations have been responsible for pushing the dollar lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the same time, traders say that they are getting prepared for action by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which calls the shots on Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . A senior Tokyo dealer said "the sentiment is that anything can happen any time and we are ready."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister ratcheted up his warnings over the rising yen Wednesday, describing its recent gain as clearly speculative and pledging to take decisive action in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if needed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have no tolerance at all for speculative movements," Jun Azumi told reporters at the finance ministry. "When it is necessary to take decisive steps I will take them, and when I say that I mean it."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He added that "the movement from yesterday is clearly driven by speculation."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market will be more worried about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the greenback falls clearly below June's low of Y77.65, but strategists say a move of that proportion appears unlikely, at least before the Fed meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some yen-dovish strategists say that even with a "QE3," the dollar won't fall below the June level because concerns over Europe are at the same time abating -- at least for now.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe's two-year slog through various sovereign debt crises has been seen as a key factor in making the yen a safe-haven.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The global market trend is for more risk taking, so I don't think the dollar will fall below the June low, even with QE3," said Osamu Takashima, chief strategist at Citibank Japan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the risk of criticism from the U.S. and Europe over renewed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , some policymakers are also looking to the BOJ to take further easing measures that would likely help weaken the yen. Lawmakers have recently stepped up their pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to be more aggressive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cabinet member Jin Matsubara, who serves as consumer affairs minister and was the head of bipartisan party to beat deflation, said in a recent interview that further easing by the BOJ is the best and quickest way to weaken the yen, calling for a higher inflation target, larger asset-buying programs and even the purchase of foreign bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "With the BOJ not doing enough easing, it's difficult to beat the strong yen," Mr. Matsubara said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Takashi Mochizuki at takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 12, 2012 03:54 ET (07:54 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120912e89c001qh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
