\par\par \b \uc2 3rd UPDATE: Asian Shares Rise; Optimism Before Fed, German Ruling\b0\par\par\uc2 833 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2012\par 10:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Asian markets advance before Fed meeting, German court ruling.\par \par \uc2 -- Nikkei rises 1.7%, Hang Seng Index adds 1.1%, S&P/ASX 200 gains 0.8%.\par \par \uc2 -- Yen strength raises \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns\par \par \uc2 (Adds information, quotes, updates/adds market levels)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Daniel Inman \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets rose on Wednesday ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting and German Constitutional Court ruling, while a stronger yen revived fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were still waiting for the week's two main risk events. The Fed's two-day policy meeting, starting Wednesday, will be keenly watched to see whether the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduces fresh stimulus measures to help the domestic economy. Focus was also on the German Constitutional Court, which will present its ruling on the legality of the European Stability Mechanism later in the global day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Market sentiment is very positive," said Brett McGonegal, chief executive officer at Reorient Financial Markets in Hong Kong, noting that markets could withstand some disappointment if either of the events fail to fully meet expectations. "Once people get into the buying mood it is not a one-day event, we could have an overall buying appetite that could absorb a shock."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar softened Tuesday in anticipation of further easing from the U.S. and a market-favorable ruling from Germany, though analysts said that the main factor contributing to dollar weakness was a warning from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service\f28 \uc2 \f2 , that it expects to reduce its triple-A credit rating for the U.S. unless it is able to tackle its debt situation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The dollar fell mostly in reaction to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  warning on U.S. sovereign credit," said Daisuke Uno, strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in Japan. "Any rating adjustment from the agency won't take effect until next year, but the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could come under even more pressure as the calendar year ends."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro remained strong against the greenback during Asian trading Wednesday, at $1.2862.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar was also stronger versus the U.S. dollar - at one point hitting $1.0472, a three week high.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar recovered against the yen on Wednesday, at Y77.80, pulling away from the 14-week low of Y77.71 hit Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The sharp rise in the yen revived fears that the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength. Speaking to reporters, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Finance Minister Jun Azumi said that "We have no tolerance at all for speculative movements."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Nikkei managed to rise despite a firm yen - the index added 1.7% to 8959.96, in part due to pre-settlement trading of futures, which helped the market as investors moved out of short positions. The rise was also led by gains in commodity-related stocks. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Metal Mining\f28 \uc2 \f2  climbed 3.3% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 JFE Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  added 3.9%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's Kospi gained 1.6% to 1950.03, as large-cap stocks edged up ahead of \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy meeting on Thursday amid growing expectations that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will cut rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In China, stocks were mixed after Chinese Premier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wen Jiabao\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday that China is on track to meet its 7.5% growth target and that he expects the economy to stabilize. The Shanghai Composite finished 0.3% up 2126.55.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index climbed 1.1% to 20075.39, with commodity stocks and Hong Kong developers outperforming. Big name local property plays - such as Cheung Kong and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Henderson Land Development\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which were up 2% and 3.1% respectively - were higher due a good response to recent property launches and diminishing property risks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's S&P/ASX 200 pushed 0.8% higher to 4361.30, with broad-based gains in mining stocks following Tuesday's rise in commodity prices. Spot iron continued to recover; Tuesday's 4.4% rise helped stocks with a focus on iron: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fortescue Metals Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  was 3% higher and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2  added 1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In corporate news, Shanghai-based carrier \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Eastern Airlines\f28 \uc2 \f2  jumped 4.3% in Hong Kong on news that it is planning to raise $570 million from its state-owned parent, the airline's second capital-raising exercise this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Communications equipment manufacturer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oki Electric Industry\f28 \uc2 \f2  tumbled 11% in Tokyo after the company disclosed that accounting improprieties in a Spanish unit resulted in Y30.8 billion worth of losses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Daniel Inman at Daniel.Inman@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TALK BAC