\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan ready for 'decisive' yen action -money chief\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2012\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Minister Nakao says \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffering due to strong yen\par \par \uc2 * Says better if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  coordinated\par \par \uc2 * Urges ECB to make good on bond-buying pledge\par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, detail, background)\par \par \uc2 By Marc Jones\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Aug 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "decisively" to combat a strong yen, which is weighing on the country's weakening economy, its top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in November. But officials have recently dropped hints of further action on concerns that a stronger yen could derail the export-dependent economy's recovery from last year's earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 "Exports have been influenced by supply chain changes and problems in Europe, some advanced economies and also in China," Takehiko Nakao, vice finance minister for international affairs, said in a speech in London.\par \par \uc2 "And we are also suffering from a very appreciated yen... If needed we will take very decisive action in the market, that is our stance."\par \par \uc2 Nakao also urged the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make good on a pledge to buy stressed European sovereign debt.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent a record 8 trillion yen ($102 billion) in unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Oct. 31, 2011 when the dollar hit a record low of 75.31 yen, and another 1 trillion yen in November on undeclared forays.\par \par \uc2 The yen had risen almost a third since 2007, gains that were proving particularly painful in the current economic environment, Nakao said.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, which has lost around 7.5 percent against the yen in the last five months, rose steadily after Nakao's comments to 78.6 yen having stood at 78.48 before he spoke.\par \par \uc2 Nakao said it was always preferential if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was done in coordination with other major powers but noted the country's recent decision to go it alone, a move he said had been criticised by its G7 partners.\par \par \uc2 Japan's economic growth rate slowed to 0.3 percent in April-June as Europe's debt crisis weighed on global demand, and economists have been trimming their forecasts for the second half of the year.\par \par \uc2 Underlining doubt over prospects for Japan's recovery, July trade data showed the sharpest drop in exports since January, in line with trends in other export-driven Asian economies .\par \par \uc2 DRAGHI URGED\par \par \uc2 Nakao said he hoped to see policy action from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is in the process of drawing up plans to shore up euro zone debt markets.\par \par \uc2 "I hope that the ECB does what Mr (Mario) Draghi has promised," he said, adding he had met with senior ECB policymakers this week, including \uc2 Jens Weidmann\uc2 , the anti-bond buying head of Germany's Bundesbank.\par \par \uc2 Draghi, the ECB president, promised last month to do "whatever it takes" to protect the euro, and the bank is expected to lay out details of its bond buying plans on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Draghi reiterated the message on Wednesday saying the ECB may have to employ "exceptional measures." Markets widely expect the ECB's new strategy to include heavy purchases of Spanish and Italian government bonds in exchange for those countries signing up for rehabilitation programmes.\par \par \uc2 Nakao praised the UK's attempts to get its finances in order rather than just spit out stimulus-based growth plans and said that Japan was also likely to opt for additional tax rises or spending cuts.\par \par \uc2 "It is a matter of common sense. If the government pays more money for pensions and medical care you should ask people to pay for it," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We need more tax measures in coming years to help government finances, but the recent move to raise consumption tax to 8 percent (from 5 percent) is an important first step."\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 78.5000 Japanese yen)\par \par \uc2 (Editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-YEN/ (UPDATE 2) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | ABN | RBN | J | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | DNP | PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120829e88t000fp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
