\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Japan's Nakao To Stay On as MOF Top  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Official for Another Year - Sources\b0\par\par\uc2 725 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2012\par 16:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 15 Aug 2012 10:50 EDT *DJ  Nakao Currently MOF Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs\par \par \uc2 15 Aug 2012 11:04 EDT DJ  Japan's Top \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Official Will Stay in Post for Another Year\par \par \uc2 --Japan's top foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bureaucrat Takehiko Nakao will stay in place for another year, sources said\par \par \uc2 --Extension of his tenure likely means \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's activist view toward \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain in place\par \par \uc2 --Yen has remained stubbornly high as investors seeks safe havens\par \par \uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi\par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Japan's top foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -policy bureaucrat, Takehiko Nakao, will stay in the post for another year to lead the nation's protracted fight against a high yen that continues to threaten a fragile economic recovery, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 The move would ensure that \uc2 Japan's Finance Ministry\uc2 , which manages the country's foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, will maintain its stance of acting against excessively sharp rises in the yen's value. The ministry is expected to announce the decision this month, those people have told Dow Jones Newswires recently.\par \par \uc2 The rise in the yen has made Japanese exports less competitive abroad and prompted many companies to shift production--and jobs--overseas. This has complicated the government's drive to help revive domestic demand and end deflation, a task already made more difficult by Europe's persistent debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Over the past five years, the dollar has fallen roughly 36% against the yen, as the late 2000s global financial crisis and the ongoing European debt turmoil have made Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  look more attractive for investors.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood around Y78.87 at 1500 GMT Wednesday, above an all-time low of Y75.31 on Oct. 31 and only slightly below big Japanese manufacturers' average in-house forecast rate for this financial year through March of Y78.95.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese counterpart of U.S. Under Secretary of the Treasury Lael Brainard and \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  executive Joerg Asmussen, Mr. Nakao has played a leading role in Tokyo's two massive rounds of solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year. The actions, which dumped a combined massive 13.6 trillion yen on the market to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , cheered Japanese manufacturers but sparked protests from the U.S. and Europe.\par \par \uc2 With domestic discontent over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistently high levels, Mr. Nakao and Finance Minister Jun Azumi have frequently warned the market in recent months that further action is on the table.\par \par \uc2 Preventing acceleration in the yen's current round of uptrend since 2007 is a major policy goal for Japanese authorities, which need solid growth to advance their economic agenda, including the planned doubling of sales taxes to slow growth in public liabilities. Government officials familiar with the matter have told Dow Jones Newswires that they will not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if that is deemed necessary to preserve a healthy economic recovery and planned tax increases--even if Washington opposes the idea.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Nakao's task remains challenging as investors continue to buy the yen as a refuge whenever renewed worries arise over Europe's turmoil and economic slowdown elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  he oversaw, the yen's current levels against the dollar are around the same as August 2011, when he was promoted to the current post through the ministry's regular summer reshuffle of career bureaucrats.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Nakao's influence over Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy could grow further after Administrative Vice Finance Minister Eijiro Katsu, the highest ranking finance bureaucrat, retires this month, some of the people said. Mr. Katsu, in contrast to many of his predecessors, has actively weighed in on international issues, including \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Last year and early 2012 there was talk within the ministry that Mr. Nakao might serve in the post only for a year, not the usual two years. But such talk has gradually faded as his policy handling, including his in-house communications and his work to help the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  build a firewall against European fallout, won high marks within the ministry, those people said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 15, 2012 11:04 ET (15:04 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120815e88f004he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
