\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Remains Firm Vs Yen Amid Mild Risk Sentiment\b0\par\par\uc2 627 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2012\par 07:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Dollar's downside vs yen supported by bids from Japanese importers, caution over \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --\uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaves benchmark interest rate unchanged\par \par \uc2 --Major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain largely in ranges\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Kosaku Narioka \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar remained firm versus the yen Tuesday in Asia as the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was sold versus other majors amid improved risk sentiment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Most Asian stock markets were mildly higher, with the Nikkei Stock Average up 0.8%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar's downside versus the yen was also supported by bids from Japanese importers and caution over potential yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Japanese authorities, Tokyo dealers said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reflecting the recent shift in the balance of trade, there were more bids from Japanese importers than offers from exporters, said Michiyoshi Kato, senior vice president of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 3.5% Tuesday, as expected. Economists say fears of further political and economic upheaval in Europe, and concerns about China's economy, will keep policy makers at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  cautious in the coming months.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Before the RBA outcome, mild risk-taking sentiment broadly prevailed, sending the yen and the dollar relatively weaker against other majors, said Motonari Ogawa, senior dealer at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have remained largely in ranges in recent days amid a lack of trading cues, with many participants away for summer holidays.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Majors meandering like this will likely continue for a little while," Mr. Ogawa said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Given continuing uncertainty over the European sovereign debt crisis and a slowdown in the emerging markets like China, the key is whether the U.S. economy can recover further, said Mizuho's Kato. "In either case, the euro/dollar will likely fall."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market focus for the rest of the day will be on Italy's industrial production for June and second-quarter gross domestic product data, as well as U.K. industrial production for June and German manufacturing orders for the same month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was at Y78.26 as of 0450 GMT from Y78.24 late Monday in New York, according to EBS. The euro was at Y97.00 from Y97.02 and $1.2396 from $1.2402.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was unchanged at CHF0.9690. The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 71.431 from 71.393. The ICE dollar index was at 82.276 from 82.254.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. pound was at $1.5590 from $1.5624.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates   