\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro May Fall Below $1.20, Y94 If Jobs Data Strong\b0\par\par\uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2012\par 07:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --US jobs data in focus, strong outcome will push euro down vs dollar, yen\par \par \uc2 --Japan MOF can create snowball effect to weak yen if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted successfully, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  says.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was little changed on Friday in Asia but investors were ready to resume selling it if U.S. jobs data due later in the day turn out to be strong because the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting outcome was disappointing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. will release its non-farm payrolls data at 1230 GMT, and a Dow Jones survey of economists forecasts that the U.S. added 95,000 jobs in July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders say a better-than-expected outcome will prompt dollar-buying, which will lead to weakening of the euro against the dollar and the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The euro may fall below $1.20 and Y94.00 today if the jobs data are strong," said Takao Yahata, chief manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at Mitsubishi UFJ Trust and Banking.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the euro was at $1.2175 from $1.2181 in New York Thursday and Y95.20 from Y95.28.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders say the euro's trend remains downward because the ECB indicated that it's ready to take action but didn't announce immediate purchase of bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The ECB may do something more to support the euro eventually, but that won't be today or tomorrow. I can't buy the euro yet," said Hiroshi Maeba, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And against the yen, the dollar's upside will be limited even if the jobs data record a strong figure, dealers say, as many speculators are waiting to make short positions around Y79.00. It was at Y78.20 as of 0450 GMT from Y78.20.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair's downside is also limited, traders say, as they believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would stage yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the greenback gets close to Y77.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The rising yen has increased deflationary pressures once again. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is on the finance ministry's agenda," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Hans Redeker. "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can develop into a snowball effect (to weaken the yen) if conducted successfully."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 72.199 from 72.200 and the ICE dollar index was at 83.325.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par USD/JPY Japan            78.18-22       78.21-25  -0.04    78.30    78.08  +1.67 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2175-78      1.2179-82  -0.03   1.2185   1.2168  -6.05 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5513-18      1.5511-16  +0.01   1.5523   1.5506  -0.17 \par U