\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Fin Min Azumi: IMF Thinking On  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Policy Similar To Japan\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mitsuru Obe   \par \uc2 128 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2012\par 02:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Japan's finance minister said Thursday that the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's view on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is similar to that of Japan.\par \par \uc2 "With respect to the current level of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, the IMF's thinking is similar to Japan's," Jun Azumi told reporters at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Azumi made the remark after the IMF, in its annual staff report on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the nation may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of volatile moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, but it should let the market determine the rate.\par \par \uc2 Write to Mitsuru Obe at mitsuru.obe@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 02-08-12 0047GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120802e88200011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
