\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Hits Two-Month Low Vs Yen as Exporters Sell\b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 2012\par 07:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Dollar falls to two-month low against yen\par \par \uc2 --Declines limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns\par \par \uc2 --Overall trading subdued ahead of FOMC outcome\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Kosaku Narioka \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell to a two-month low against the yen Wednesday in Asia on the back of selling by Japanese exporters, but trading was generally quiet as market participants wait for a Federal Open Market Committee meeting later in the global day.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell to Y77.90 at one point as exporter selling triggered stop-loss orders below Y78.00, Tokyo dealers said. But the greenback didn't extend its declines as caution over potential market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese authorities prevailed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overall trading was subdued ahead of the closely watched FOMC meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets speculate that the Fed could take new action to spur growth, such as buying mortgages or government securities to bring down long-term interest rates, or simply promise to do more later if necessary. Officials may take the option of waiting until September, when they will formally update their economic forecasts, before deciding on anything significant.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shuichi Kanehira, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said that although he doesn't expect major steps from the Fed this time, "(the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) is unlikely to do anything that disappoints markets."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The key is whether the FOMC statement hints at easing at the next meeting," said Osao Iizuka, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "If that happens, the dollar will be sold."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even so, the dollar will likely decline only gradually against the yen amid caution over potential yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, a senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not considering foreign bond purchases as a monetary policy option.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Buying and selling of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at producing a similar effect to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the remit of the finance minister," BOJ Executive Director \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kazuo Momma\f28 \uc2 \f2  told a lower house finance committee. The comments came after new BOJ policy board member \f28 \uc2 \f2 Takehiro Sato\f28 \uc2 \f2  said last week that the BOJ buying overseas bonds would be one way to help lower Japan's real interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Although Momma's remarks were significant, widespread caution ahead of the FOMC meeting meant that there was no immediate reaction in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was at Y78.02 as of 0450 GMT from Y78.12 late Tuesday in New York, according to EBS.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was at $1.2292 from $1.2304 and was at Y95.91 from Y96.11. The greenback was at CHF0.9771 from CHF0.9764.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. pound was at $1.5663 from $1.5678.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 71.69 from 71.67. The ICE Dollar index was at 82.693 from 82.658.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            78.00-04       78.11-13  -0.13    78.16    77.94  +1.44 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2290-94      1.2302-05  -0.09   1.2304   1.2282  -5.16 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5661-66      1.5673-79  -0.08   1.5679   1.5658  +0.78 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9770-74      0.9761-66  +0.08   0.9780   0.9764  +4.26 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.0025-30      1.0030-35  -0.05   1.0040   1.0026  -1.79 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0486-90      1.0501-05  -0.14   1.0502   1.0466  +2.74 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.8107-12      0.8084-89  +0.28   0.8114   0.8084  +4.29 \par  \par Euro Rate \par EUR/JPY Japan            95.88-92       96.10-15  -0.23    96.13    95.72  -3.68 \par  \par Source: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICAP PLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Kosaku Narioka at kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2 \f2  [ 01-08-12 0530GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120801e881000ay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
