\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA: For the Yen, It Could Again Be a Hot August\b0\par\par\uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2012\par 11:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- August has traditionally been a period of yen strength over the past decade\par \par \uc2 -- Yen may rise this year as well if risk-aversion intensifies or even on self-fulfillment market moves\par \par \uc2 -- Dollar at Y77.00-Y77.50 a likely support level due to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--The safe-haven yen has been a summer-haven for the past decade, and traders say that global money may again look to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unless warned off by the threat of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo traders say the dollar, currently at Y78.27 as of 0907 GMT, may fall to Y77.00 in August, adding that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk would rise if the dollar begins to trade around the Y77.50 level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The seasonal strengthening of the yen has been well-charted phenomenon in the market. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Masafumi Yamamoto said the yen has posted its biggest monthly gain in August every year since 1999, except in 2006 and 2008 when it weakened.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A traditional explanation for the tendency is that Japanese institutional investors repatriate money from the redemption of \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds, with the impact magnified amid the thin summer market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Whether such flows have been behind the yen's rise remains unclear, but non-Japanese short-term-focused speculators often used the talk as an excuse to target the yen, Tokyo traders say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More recently, August has often been a month with major news that favors the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In 2007, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  froze its funds due to the U.S. sub-prime mortgage market crisis, followed by September 2008's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lehman Brothers\f28 \uc2 \f2  collapse. Hirohisa Fujii, who soon became finance minister, made repeated remarks suggesting tolerance toward the strong yen in August 2009. August 2010 saw growing worries about the U.S. economic outlook and 2011 was when the U.S. lost its triple-A credit rating from S&P.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the coming month, the yen-positive risks include this Thursday's \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy-setting meeting and Friday's non-farm payrolls data. The current high yield on Spanish sovereign bonds also cannot be ignored, traders say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders added that even if these risk events do not unfold, the yen may still rise because investors believe the yen is supposed to rise in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Minister Jun Azumi, who's aware of the summer yen tendency, warned the market by signaling the possibility of yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's no economic reason for the yen to rise in the Summer," Mr. Azumi said Tuesday, adding that he is watching the market with "heightened sense of caution" and will take decisive action if necessary.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback has quietly been traded around Y78.15 recently, and that's because investors fear that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will stage yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the dollar falls sharply.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I see a realistic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  possibility when the dollar is below Y78.00," one trader said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many Tokyo traders say the next key level is at Y77.65, the low marked after the disappointing U.S. non-farm payrolls data released on June 1. Many traders say the Bank of Japan conducted a rate-check with Japanese banks at that time, a severe warning by the authorities which can be followed by actual yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the finance ministry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For this reason, traders say the market will be cautious about pushing the yen too high, saying that a Y77.00-Y77.50 range is the likely floor for the greenback in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Takashi Mochizuki at takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2 \f2  [ 31-07-12 0944GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120731e87v0011k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
