\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Weakens Ahead of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Meetings\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicole Hong   \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 2012\par 23:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global FX & Fixed Income News\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The euro traded lower against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday as concerns mounted that a \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting later this week would fall short of expectations.\par \par \uc2 The euro ended the New York session at $1.2260, down from $1.2322 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched a three-week high against the dollar after ECB President Mario Draghi said the bank would do whatever it takes to save the euro zone. However, last week's optimism began to unwind as investors wondered if Mr. Draghi's proposal would be able to garner wider support among European policy makers at an ECB policy meeting Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The euro-zone crisis has been rumbling along for three years, and European policy makers have promised much and delivered little," said Richard Franulovich, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp\uc2 . in New York, adding that he expects "underwhelming" results from Thursday's meeting.\par \par \uc2 Analysts widely anticipate an ECB interest-rate cut Thursday but are uncertain about the size of the cut or whether it will be accompanied by a deposit-rate cut.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders didn't take aggressive positions ahead of the coming \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings and U.S. nonfarm payrolls data due later this week. The Federal Open Market Committee concludes its two-day policy meeting Wednesday, when investors will be looking for hints of further easing.\par \par \uc2 Economists largely expect the Fed to wait until September before launching another round of bond buying. Anyone looking for aggressive Fed action this week "will ultimately be disappointed" because the Fed will likely wait for two more rounds of labor market and economic data before it acts, Citi analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Also, the Bank of England's policy meeting concludes Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was weaker against the yen, recently trading at Y78.17 from Y78.44 late Friday. The euro was also sharply lower at Y95.83 from Y96.64.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen strength until the dollar falls below Y76, near the level when the BoJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October 2011, said Shahab Jalinoos, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is under global political criticism for being a "serial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervener\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," suggesting the BoJ may choose to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by expanding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quantitative-easing program instead of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly, Mr. Jalinoos added.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Australian dollar was up against the dollar after rallying to a four-month high of $1.0511 earlier. The Aussie recently fetched $1.0503 from $1.0484 late Friday.\par \par \uc2 The pound traded lower against the dollar at $1.5710, compared with $1.5748 late Friday. The dollar was also strong against the Swiss franc at CHF0.9797 from CHF0.9748.\par \par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, which measures the dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , closed the session at 71.77, up from 71.67.\par \par \uc2 -Laura Clarke contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Nicole Hong at nicole.hong@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 07-30-12 1706ET ]\par \par \uc2 1074 1863 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020120730e87u0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
