\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Keeps Up Rhetoric Against Strong Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2012\par 04:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Japan's finance, economy ministers keep up rhetoric against strong yen\par \par \uc2 --Finance minister says excessive rises in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be dealt with by drawing on all policy measures\par \par \uc2 --Economy minister says rising concern over European debt crisis also strengthening yen\par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Japan's finance and economy ministers kept up their efforts to talk down the yen Tuesday, as the market remained somewhat cautious over a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's strength.\par \par \uc2 Finance minister Jun Azumi said he will draw on all policy measures to counter any excessive rises in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It is clear that the recent, one-sided climb in the yen is not reflecting the real state of Japan's economy," he said at a press conference after a regular cabinet meeting. "We will closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements with a greater sense of caution from now. We will not rule out any measures against excessive moves and will take decisive action when that's deemed necessary."\par \par \uc2 Economy minister Motohisa Furukawa also said that rising concerns over the European debt crisis, especially with regard to Spain, are fueling increased risk-aversion, global stock falls and a soaring yen.\par \par \uc2 "Concern over Europe is expanding and these worries are leading to increased risk-off sentiment in markets, our current strengthening yen and global stock falls," Motohisa Furukawa said at a separate press conference.\par \par \uc2 Growing worries over Europe's debt crisis in light of the Spanish government's worsening fiscal state have been piling pressure on the euro and sending investors flocking to the safe-haven yen.\par \par \uc2 Furukawa said the concerns could put pressure on the Japanese economy by driving up the yen and causing excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and falls in stock prices.\par \par \uc2 "We need to watch the situation closely and take decisive measures when necessary," he said.\par \par \uc2 As of 0200 GMT, the dollar was at Y78.22 and the euro was at Y94.87.\par \par \uc2 Referring to the Cabinet's decision earlier Tuesday to approve the appointment of two new members to the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's policy board, Furukawa said the appointments were appropriate.\par \par \uc2 "We hope the new members perform their duties well," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Cabinet appointed Nomura Securities Chief Economist \uc2 Takahide Kiuchi\uc2  and Morgan Stanley MUFG Securities Chief Japan Economist \uc2 Takehiro Sato\uc2  as members of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's highest decision-making body. The two will hold a press conference from 0800 GMT Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Alexander Martin at alexander.martin@dowjones.com and Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 07-23-12 2255ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020120724e87o0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
