\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar, Euro Relatively Steady Against Yen Over  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears\b0\par\par\uc2 768 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2012\par 07:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Dollar, euro stable against yen over conern of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  finance minister says decisive action would be taken when necessary to stem yen's rise\par \par \uc2 --Euro remains pressured from Euro crisis, Spain worries\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Alexander Martin \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar and euro remained relatively stable against the yen during Asian trading Tuesday, as concerns over a potential \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen's strength kept the yen-crosses from sliding lower.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese authorities also kept up their rhetoric against the rising yen as the dollar fell below Y78.00 on Monday to hit Y77.94, its lowest level since June 1. The euro also traded as low as Y94.23 Monday, its lowest level against the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since November 2000.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is clear that the recent, one-sided climb in the yen is not reflecting the real state of Japan's economy," said Finance Minister Jun Azumi at a press conference Tuesday after a regular Cabinet meeting. "We will closely watch \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements with a greater sense of caution from now. We will not rule out any measures against excessive moves and will take decisive action when that's deemed necessary."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While market participants did not expect the MOF to step in to the market anytime soon, some said more verbal warnings, as well as so-called unannounced "stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " could take place if the dollar dips below the Y78.00 level.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will take place unless the dollar enters the Y76 level, but there is greater possibility of authorities stepping up verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as well as implementing stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as it enters the Y77 level," said Junichi Ishikawa, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at IG Market Securities in Tokyo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro in the meanwhile also remained pressured by concern over Spain's fiscal health and as Greece faces new financial troubles. Spain's borrowing costs climbed to a euro-era high Monday as yields on Spanish 10-year bonds hit 7.59% at one point. There were also concern that more regions in Spain may need to tap government funds, increasing fears that the Spanish bank bailout agreed last month might not be enough to stem the ongoing debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In addition, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Investors Services revised to negative from stable its outlooks on the sovereign ratings of Germany, the Netherlands and Luxembourg.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And with Spain scheduled to auction three and six-month bills later in the day, "the outcome may highlight a greater threat for contagion and the ongoing turmoil in Europe may continue to sap risk-taking behavior as the EU maintains a reactionary approach in addressing the debt crisis," said David Song, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Analyst at DailyFX.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We anticipate to see fresh yearly lows in the euro/dollar as European policy makers struggle to restore investor confidence," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the dollar was slightly lower at Y78.25 from Y78.40 late New York trading Monday, according to trading platform EBS. The euro was at $1.2126 from $1.2117 while it was at Y94.91 from Y94.98.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE dollar index, which tracks the dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was trading at 83.684 from 83.478.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Wall Street Journal Dollar Index, another measure of the dollar's broad value, was at 72.53 from 72.61.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par  \par                            Latest       Previous   %Chg    Daily    Daily   %Chg \par Dollar Rates                               Close            High      Low  12/31 \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Japan            78.24-28       78.37-41  -0.17    78.40    78.22  +1.75 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2125-28      1.2115-18  +0.08   1.2138   1.2110  -6.43 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5528-32      1.5505-09  +0.15   1.5534   1.5502  -0.08 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9902-06      0.9909-13  -0.07   0.9917   0.9896  +5.67 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.0181-86      1.0186-91  -0.05   1.0192   1.0178  -0.26 \par AUD/USD Australia       1.0302-04      1.0257-61  +0.43   1.0308   1.0252  +0.93 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.7916-18      0.7872-78  +0.54   0.7921   0.7876  +1.81 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan            94.88-92       94.96-05  -0.08    95.01    94.82  -4.68 \par  \par Source: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICAP PLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Alexander Martin at alexander.martin@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=dj