\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Unchanged Vs Yen, May Fall On QE3 Hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2012\par 07:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Dollar may fall below Y78.00 On the Fed QE3 anticipation, traders say\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns may rise if greenback falls below Y78.50\par \par \uc2 --Euro likely to fall more on popular euro-carry trade\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar was almost unchanged against the yen on Friday in Asia amid concerns by some market participants about another Japanese government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it will likely start to fall as the market as a whole factors in another easing by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback was at 78.62 yen as of 0450 GMT from Y78.59 in New York Thursday. It rose to as high as Y78.80 on some Japanese companies' M&A-related flows, but the upward move soon lost momentum as investors saw large dollar-selling interest by Japanese exporters around Y79.00, traders say.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Non-Japanese traders say they see the risk of a yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  increasing once the unit falls below Y78.50, with some even saying there are rumors that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is placing stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  orders below the mark, which Japanese traders don't buy at all.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears, the dollar is likely to fall, traders say, because the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as a whole is anticipating another round of Fed easing, often referred to as QE3.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Recent U.S. economic indicators are all weak and Treasury yields are decreasing, but stock and commodity markets are rising," Citibank Japan's chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Osamu Takashima. "All explain the market's expectations for the QE3, and the dollar is just following that trend."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Takashima said the greenback may fall below Y78.00 in the near term.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the euro was at $1.2258 from $1.2280 and Y96.37 from Y96.50.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ever since the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its overnight deposit rate to zero earlier this month, the market trend is to fund in the euro and to buy higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Australian dollar, a tactic called euro-carry trade. That means the euro is also under downward pressure against the dollar and the yen as well.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The WSJ Dollar Index, which tracks the dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , ended the New York trading day at 71.96 from 71.88, while the ICE Dollar Index was at 82.978\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par USD/JPY Japan            78.60-64       78.57-61  +0.04    78.80    78.58  +2.22 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2256-60      1.2279-82  -0.18   1.2283   1.2252  -5.42 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5703-08      1.5722-27  -0.12   1.5725   1.5698  +1.05 \par USD/CHF Switzerland