\par\par \b \uc2 IMF head hails Japan tax hike plan, urges more steps to fix debt\b0\par\par\uc2 199 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2012\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 6 (Reuters) - The head of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said on Friday Japan's plan to raise its sales tax is appropriate and timely but more measures should be taken to fix its public finances.\par \par \uc2 IMF Managing Director \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 , speaking at a news conference, also welcomed the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to cut its deposit rate, calling it an important step to activate interbank markets.\par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut its main interest rate to a record low on Thursday to prop up a deteriorating euro zone economy and reduced its deposit rate, which acts as a floor for the money market, to zero from 0.25 percent.\par \par \uc2 Lagarde also said the yen was moderately overvalued. When asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case of rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings, she said it would be justifiable if Japan duly consulted with other countries.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Stanley White and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 IMF-LAGARDE/JAPAN-TAX (URGENT) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | G | RBN | J | NAT | ABN | UKI | RNP | DNP | PTD | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120706e876000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
