\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE: Japan Finance Minister Vows to Defend Economy From Europe Fallout\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2012\par 12:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Japan finance minister vows to protect economy from Europe crisis so Tokyo can raise sales taxes.\par \par \uc2 (Adds Azumi comments in 3rd paragraph, Japan government official remarks in 6th, 7th, 11th paragraph) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Nakamichi \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--Japan's finance minister on Tuesday pledged to prevent Europe's debt crisis from derailing the nation's economic recovery or its planned fiscal overhaul, in another indication of his resolve to fend off overseas economic problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe's fiscal woes remain a major drag on Japan's export-reliant economy as it exerts upward pressure on the yen and continues to take the steam out of the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There are various downside risks stemming from Europe," Jun Azumi said after the nation's lower house of parliament passed the bill to raise the 5% consumption tax to 10% by 2015.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We must make efforts to prevent firm movement in our domestic demand from stalling" so the government can implement planned tax increases, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Azumi's comments could add to speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market if speculators cause the yen to rise sharply, undermining Japanese recovery and making tax increases in the future more difficult. Failure to implement sales tax hikes could stoke doubts over Japan's ability to rein in its public debt--now more than twice its annual economic output--and spark growth-choking surges in borrowing costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ministry may consider any sharp yen gains in the coming few days to be speculation-driven. That's partly because the ministry's recent in-house hearings with banks has left it the impression that dollar selling by Japanese exporters for the April-June quarter has mostly run its course, according to a Japanese government official.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ministry views that Japanese exporters completed much of such transactions when the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  temporarily rose above 80 yen on Friday and Monday, the official said.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has held off on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the yen's strength since early November amid speculation that signs of U.S. displeasure at its solo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last year may keep it too wary of acting again. But Tokyo officials have hardened their commentary in recent weeks, signaling their preparedness to take "appropriate actions" on the yen if deemed necessary, even if the U.S. is opposed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials have taken heart from the International Monetary Fund's recent acknowledgment that the yen is "moderately overvalued." The fund also shows sympathy toward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth abrupt gains in the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government official also noted that inflows of funds from foreign investors seeking refuge in the yen from Europe's crisis can be categorized as one of "negative spillovers" that the Group of 20 industrial and developing economies have recently vowed to "minimize." Moves by investors to seek safe-haven have been a major reason for the yen's rapid climb over recent years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 26, 2012 06:22 ET (10:22 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120626e86q002mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
