\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW:Ex-BOJ Muto: BOJ Buying JGBs With Longer Maturities An Option\b0\par\par\uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2012\par 07:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Former BOJ Deputy Gov. Toshiro Muto says buying government bonds with longer maturities an option for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 -- Says fine for BOJ to buy JGBs beyond current self-imposed limit\par \par \uc2 -- Says opposed to idea of BOJ buying foreign bonds\par \par \uc2 -- Says yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  possible if dollar falls to Y75-Y76\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Megumi Fujikawa and Tatsuo Ito \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  should consider stepping up its purchases of domestic government bonds, especially notes with longer maturities, if the European debt crisis takes a serious turn for the worse or another threat to the nation's economic outlook emerges, former Deputy Gov. Toshiro Muto said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Since the financial markets have reacted sensitively to the BOJ's policy steps in the past, (buying JGBs with longer maturities) would have quite a big impact on the markets," the current \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daiwa Institute of Research\f28 \uc2 \f2  chairman told Dow Jones Newswires in a recent interview.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Muto, who is seen as a strong contender to become the next BOJ governor, also said he doesn't think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's self-imposed rule on keeping its government bond holdings below the amount of banknotes in circulation should serve as an obstacle preventing it from taking necessary steps.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concerned that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rampant purchases of JGBs are being perceived as monetization, Gov. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Masaaki Shirakawa\f28 \uc2 \f2  has repeatedly emphasized the dangers stemming from a continuation of its sovereign debt buying campaign.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The BOJ's JGB holdings will likely exceed 83 trillion yen of bank notes in circulation for the first time ever next December. But that amount includes Y24 trillion in JGBs that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is committed to buying by the end of this year under its asset-purchase program, which is exempt from the so-called "banknote rule."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the BOJ's policy board is expected to vote to keep its monetary policy on hold at the end of its two-day meeting on Friday, Mr. Muto said that the bank will likely be forced to take additional steps in the months ahead if the euro-zone turmoil drags on.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The BOJ is heading to the (June) meeting at a very difficult time and will be pressed to make a very difficult decision," he said about the meeting that is scheduled just a few days before Greece's closely-watched elections.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Muto served as a deputy BOJ governor from 2003 to 2008. Although the government tapped him in 2008 to head the bank, his nomination was voted down in parliament due to concerns about his ties to finance ministry, where he spent most of his career.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, times have changed and many key policymakers in the ruling Democratic Party of Japan, which voted against Mr. Muto's nomination, aren't openly opposed to the idea of him succeeding Shirakawa, whose term expires next April.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With the yen still under upward pressure amid uncertainties in Europe, the notion of the BOJ buying foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denominated bonds as part of its monetary easing has been in the spotlight recently.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But Mr. Muto said he's against the proposal as it could jeopardize Japan's relationship with other nations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Global markets will perceive the BOJ's purchases of foreign bonds as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , even if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  calls it monetary easing," he warned.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In any case, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  has the authority to directly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if it sees any excessive moves in the yen, Mr. Muto said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely be justified to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if the yen strengthens to a level incompatible with the economic fundamentals," he said. "I think that the yen could try Y75-Y76 (against the dollar), and this would be the time to consider \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar stood at Y79.64 as of 0521 GMT Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Megumi Fujikawa at megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com [ 13-06-12 0553GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120613e86d0008b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
