\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/JPY Rises On IMF Comments; 80.00 Cap - Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2012\par 05:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0356 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY rises after a senior IMF official says the fund is sympathetic to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's views on the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out sharp market moves. "If market forces lead to disruptive flows, short-term smoothing is something that we would understand," says David Lipton, the fund's First Deputy Managing Director. The IMF report saying that the BOJ's asset purchase program could be expanded substantially also raised expectations for additional easing measures by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says a senior dealer at a major Japanese trust bank. The USD/JPY is at 79.54, after rising to 79.60. The pair may rise to 80.00, but offers above that level will likely serve resistance, the dealer says.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 12-06-12 0356GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120612e86c00057\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
