\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Gives Back Gains As Doubts Emerge About ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2012\par 07:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Euro gives back all its overnight night gains as markets begin to doubt the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment to tackling the debt crisis\par \par \uc2 --The risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities retreats with the dollar above Y77.50, dealer says\par \par \uc2 --Swiss data may indicate the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't hold the line by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market indefinitely\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--The euro slipped against the dollar in Asia Thursday as investors interpreted the outcome of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy meeting overnight as indicating the authority may be reluctant to take decisive action to tackle the region's debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ECB kept its key policy rate unchanged at 1.0% Wednesday, although its head, Mario Draghi, suggested more easing may be in store.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The ECB failed to deliver a positive surprise," said Atsuo Ogaki, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Japan at Nomura Securities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of 0450 GMT, the euro was at $1.2562 down from a high of $1.2587 marked in New York after the ECB meeting. Against the yen, it was at Y99.77 from Y99.66.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I was surprised that the euro rose more than what I had expected on the ECB outcome. But the follow-through moves proved it was just investors' position adjustment," Mr. Ogaki said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors said there was more downside potential for the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the run-up to Greece's election later this month. One dealer said European investors may resume selling when they enter the market later in the day, pushing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down further.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar, meanwhile, was at Y79.42 from Y79.21. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 82.274 from 82.150.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors will pay attention to remarks by Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke later in the day for hints of additional Fed easing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Trading in the dollar against the yen was subdued, as investors remained cautious about possible Japanese yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But not many Tokyo investors believe the risk is especially high at the moment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely with the dollar at least above Y77.50," Mr. Ogaki said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, market participants will pay attention to Switzerland's foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve data for May, due at 0700 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Junya Tanase expects the figure will increase by at least 20 billion Swiss francs due to continued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise. But such an outcome would mean franc-buying pressure is strong in the market and the SNB may be unable to hold the line through indefinite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "That will increase the risk of the euro falling sharply below CHF1.20, the SNB's key defense line," Mr. Tanase said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par                                     2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par Dollar Rates \par USD/JPY Japan            79.40-42       79.17-21  +0.28    79.43    79.18  +3.24 \par EUR/USD Euro            1.2562-64      1.2580-83  -0.15   1.2585   1.2558  -3.06 \par GBP/USD U.K.            1.5473-78      1.5494-99  -0.14   1.5498   1.5470  -0.43 \par USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9559-64      0.9541-46  +0.19   0.9563   0.9544  +2.02 \par USD/CAD Canada          1.0277-82      1.0273-79  +0.04   1.0292   1.0268  +0.68 \par AUD/USD Australia       0.9950-54      0.9927-31  +0.23   0.9966   0.9886  -2.51 \par NZD/USD New Zealand     0.7704-10      0.7705-11  -0.01   0.7715   0.7688  -0.89 \par  \par Euro Rate \par  \par EUR/JPY Japan            99.75-78       99.61-66  +0.13    99.89    99.58  +0.21 \par  \par Source: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICAP PLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Takashi Mochizuki at takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 07-06-12 0542GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120607e8670007x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
