\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Says G-7 Has 'No Objection' to Actions Against Strong Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2012\par 17:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Japan Finance Minister Azumi says G-7 partners voiced no objections to potential actions against a strong yen\par \par \uc2 --Remarks came after conference call of the group's finance ministers and central bankers\par \par \uc2 --Statement sends dollar higher against yen in view that it strengthens \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hand in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi and Tatsuo Ito\par \par \uc2 TOKYO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister said Tuesday that the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations voiced "no objection" to his calls during a teleconference for standing against undue exchange-rate volatility and acting together as appropriate on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The remarks from Finance Minister Jun Azumi sent the yen lower in the view that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have more leeway to again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. That pushed the dollar to just under the Y79.00 mark from Y78.25 before Mr. Azumi's comments.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo has been again threatening to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to put a halt to the yen's rise, which poses problems for its big export-oriented manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 "We have a sense of crisis" over the strong yen, Mr. Azumi told reporters after a teleconference of G-7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs.\par \par \uc2 "I told them that we want them to reaffirm the agreement over \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The view I wanted them to share is that excess volatility or disorderly movement in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has adverse effects on economic and financial stability and that we will closely discuss moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and respond appropriately. There was no objection to that," he said.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts saw the statement as increasing the chance for market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  gets a green light to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  said in an email to clients in the wake of the G-7 talks.\par \par \uc2 But it wasn't clear if the other G-7 nations shared that view. The E.U. and U.S. have in the past voiced concerns about Japan's forays into the market, stressing the group's commitment to letting the market determine exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Azumi declined to comment on whether he has informed the rest of the G-7--the U.S., Germany, France, the U.K., Italy, Canada--of his policy to take "decisive steps" on the yen if needed. The phrase is a Japanese code for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There was no statement issued by the group after the conference call nor any immediate post-discussion remarks from other participants.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long struggled to win approval for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Europe and the U.S. Before Mr. Azumi's news conference, few \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders and analysts had predicted that the U.S. or the E.U. nations would back Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Azumi also said that the G-7 shared views on Europe's debt crisis, which he said was the main topic of discussion.\par \par \uc2 European officials "said they will handle the issues, including Spain's debt problems, in a responsible manner, and I trust them," he said.\par \par \uc2 But he remained vague on whether European officials pledged any new measures, only saying, "I said I want them to take detailed steps in a successive fashion to make not only us but also the market feel safe."\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com [ 06-05-12 1122ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120605e865000be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
