\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/ \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Real Time: Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Watch: Real, and Symbolic\b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 2012\par 11:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Japan Real Time Report blog at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki\par \par \uc2 With the yen resuming its ascent against the dollar, markets are once again on high alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese government.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Video: Europe is Biggest Risk to Japanese Economy -- PM Noda \par  \par    -- Stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : When Ministers Act...in Secret \par  \par    -- Is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Accepting Yen Reality? \par  \par    -- \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  101: The BOJ Rate Check \par  \par    -- Honda CFO Raises Eyebrow at \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Timing \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In that environment, JRT thought it would be useful to dust off its handy-dandy guide for readers on different types of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There's real \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , when the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  orders the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy dollars in the market, to prop up the value of the greenback. And then there's symbolic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , when BOJ traders call around in the market asking about dollar-buying prices -- in hopes that the word gets around and markets get the message, before the BOJ actually has to execute any trades.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As we explained during a prior period of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  watch last summer, that can also be effective in moving markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That drama was replicated Friday night Japan time, shortly after the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics reported surprisingly weak jobs data. The dollar slipped suddenly against the yen, from \u165\'00\'A578.05 to \u165\'00\'A577.65 -- and then suddenly shot up, within 18 minutes hitting \u165\'00\'A578.72.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Why the jump? It wasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  per se, traders said. But two said that the BOJ made a round of calls to financial institutions asking about the latest dollar/yen price, the Wall Street Journal reported Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Yes there was," one trader said when asked about BOJ queries. This trader and another said that while the BOJ asked for the latest dollar/yen price, it didn't actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by saying "mine" when told the price.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 . \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 04-06-12 0922GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120604e864000fb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
