\par\par \b \uc2 DJ WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Euro Advances Ahead Of G-7 Talks; Yen Slips -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Erin McCarthy   \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2012\par 00:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The euro edged higher Monday as upcoming talks between global finance ministers and a meeting of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later this week helped drive optimism for further measures to ease stresses in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 In the short term, investors are looking ahead to a teleconference among Group of Seven finance ministers Tuesday. That call is expected to largely focus on the situation in Spain, where a banking and fiscal crisis has kept markets on edge.\par \par \uc2 Also lifting sentiment, later this week, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its rate-setting meeting, where it is widely expected to cut its key policy rate by 25 basis points. Some analysts say there is an increased chance that the ECB could announce another round of liquidity injections into Europe's financial system, through long-term refinancing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or LTROs.\par \par \uc2 "The likelihood of the ECB doing something in the near term has gone up," said Aroop Chatterjee, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  quantitative strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Such projections led investors to pare their antieuro bets, though the trading was light as London traders stayed away from their desks to celebrate the Queen's jubilee.\par \par \uc2 In addition, signs that the euro zone could eventually shift toward broader European supervision of systematically important banks, and perhaps even a banking union, lifted market hopes. German Chancellor Angela Merkel on Monday said European leaders will discuss European supervision of "systemically relevant banks" at a summit later this month.\par \par \uc2 The euro traded at $1.2502 Monday from $1.2435 late Friday, according to EBS via CQG. Against the Swiss franc, the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  held steady just above the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's floor of CHF1.20, trading at CHF1.2010 from CHF1.2012 Friday.\par \par \uc2 Despite Monday's optimism, the euro's gains could be short-lived given the various risks remaining in the euro-zone debt crisis, including the Greek national elections later this month, traders say.\par \par \uc2 "There's no conviction that [the euro's] going to go higher," said Douglas Borthwick, managing director of Faros Trading in Stamford, Conn. The euro will likely trade in its current range against the dollar "with a negative bias, as long as there's no action" from European policymakers, he added.\par \par \uc2 In addition, while speculators and hedge fund managers have unwound some short-term bets against the euro recently, real money investors will continue to pare their holdings of the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say.\par \par \uc2 As \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the euro rebounded, the classic safe-harbor Japanese yen weakened amid concerns that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen in the near term. On Friday, the Bank of Japan checked rates in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, seen as a warning shot for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen's strength continues. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  prefers a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so its manufacturers and exporters can remain competitive.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at was at Y97.93 from Y96.99, while the dollar was at Y78.35 from Y78.03.\par \par \uc2 Against the Swiss franc, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at CHF0.9608 from CHF0.9664. The U.K. pound was at $1.5380 from $1.5347.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at about 82.539 from about 82.890.\par \par \uc2 --Matthew Walter contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Erin McCarthy at erin.mccarthy@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020120604e864009yd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
